--TEST--
an enum case is a PascalCase declaration site like the enum itself, and every mis-cased case is reported — `rule:core-api/casing-checks-the-leading-character`
--FILE--
<?nvs
enum Level {
    low,
    high,
}
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0110]: `low` must be PascalCase, e.g. `Low`
  --> case.nvs:3:5
%A
error[E0110]: `high` must be PascalCase, e.g. `High`
  --> case.nvs:4:5
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
